    "title": "NASA GISTEMP",
    "category": "data",
    "short": "NASA GISS's monthly global temperature record, land plus ocean, since 1880.",
    "body": "The Goddard Institute for Space Studies combines thousands of weather stations and ship/buoy sea temperatures into a global average and publishes how far each month is from the 1951-1980 average.\n\n**Limits.** Monthly, published around the 10th of the next month, and recent months can be revised slightly. It is a global average, not a forecast for Samui.",
    "howToRead": "Numbers are degC above the 1951-1980 average. August 2026 was +1.40. The yearly tropical band (24S-24N) is published only once a year is complete.",
