    "title": "NASA GMAO GEOS-S2S forecast plumes",
    "category": "data",
    "short": "NASA's own seasonal model forecast of the Nino regions and the Indian Ocean Dipole.",
    "body": "NASA's Global Modeling and Assimilation Office runs the GEOS-S2S-3 coupled model several times a month and publishes plume charts once a month: Nino 3.4, 3, 4, 1+2 and the Indian Ocean Dipole for the next 9 months.\n\n**Limits.** Images only: NASA does not publish the numbers in a machine-readable form, so none are extracted. Released early each month (September 2026 posted on 2 Sep).",
    "howToRead": "Each dashed line is one model start date, the thick red line their average. Values are degC from normal. The September 2026 release keeps Nino 3.4 near +3.5 to +3.8 through December before a slow decline.",
