    "body": "NASA Worldview can render any GIBS satellite layer as one image for a chosen area and day. Every 6 hours the app builds 5 such images, downloads each one to make sure it really contains data (an empty day is a tiny black picture), and lists only the good ones.\n\n**Limits.** Polar-orbiting satellites pass once or twice a day; clouds hide the ground in true colour. If a day has no data the previous day is used, and the date says so.",
