    "short": "The European centre's monthly seasonal forecast of the Nino 3.4 temperature anomaly for the next 6 months, as a chart.",
    "body": "Each month ECMWF runs its SEAS5 seasonal model 51 times with slightly different starting states. The plume chart shows every run's Nino 3.4 anomaly: thin red lines are the forecasts, the dashed line the observations. Two versions are kept: absolute and relative (RONI-like) index.\n\n**Limits.** A picture, not numbers: we store the chart link only. Model forecasts made in spring are less reliable (spring barrier). Chart (c) ECMWF, CC-BY-4.0.",
    "howToRead": "If most lines stay above +2 C, a very strong El Nino is forecast to continue; the spread of the lines is the uncertainty. Status key ecmwf_nino_plume {issued, label, images}.",
