    "short": "ERA5 rain vs normal first; if ERA5 is missing, the forecast model's own past-day analyses; plus PWA notices, the dam and the seasonal forecast.",
    "body": "The level comes from rain over 90 days (180 in the dry season) as a percentage of the 1991-2020 ERA5 normal. If the ERA5 archive is missing or more than 10 days behind, the app uses Open-Meteo's past-day model analyses against the same normal and says so. PWA Ko Samui notices, the Ratchaprapa dam (mainland, regional only) and the ECMWF SEAS5 3-month forecast can raise the level.\n\n**Limits.** The island's own reservoir levels and the PWA rotation schedule are not published in machine-readable form. Check them on the PWA notices page (branch Ko Samui) or call PWA 1662.",
